agraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Active surveillance", "runs": [{"text": "Active"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "surveillance"}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "413"}}, {"id": "body-25108", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Surgery (curative or palliative)", "runs": [{"text": "Surgery"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(curative"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "palliative)"}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "413"}}, {"id": "body-25109", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Surgery", "runs": [{"text": "Surgery"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-25110", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "\nRadiotherapy (curative or palliative)", "runs": [{"text": "\n"}, {"text": "Radiotherapy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(curative"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "palliative)"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "413"}}, {"id": "body-25111", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Hormonal therapy (chemical vs surgical castration)", "runs": [{"text": "Hormonal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "therapy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(chemical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "surgical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "castration)"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "413"}}, {"id": "body-25112", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Chemotherapy", "runs": [{"text": "Chemotherapy"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "413"}}, {"id": "body-25114", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Early stages (Low and Intermediate risk groups) can be treated with either radical prostatectomy or radical Radiotherapy with cure intent. However, surgery may cause postoperative impotence and impaired urinary control. TURP is carried out to both confirm the diagnosis and also as part of relieving obstruction.", "runs": [{"text": "Early stages (Low and Intermediate risk groups) can be treated with either radical prostatectomy or radical Radiotherapy with cure intent. However, surgery may cause postoperative impotence and impaired urinary control. TURP is carried out to both confirm the diagnosis and also as part of relieving obstruction."}]}, {"id": "body-25116", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Radiotherapy", "runs": [{"text": "Radiotherapy"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-25117", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Radical Radiotherapy for Adjuvant and definitive, EBRT up to 74 Gy/37 Fractions can be given using 3DCRT or IMRT Techniques. Palliative radiotherapy is valuable to bone metastases, massive hematuria, spinal cord compression and brain metastases", "runs": [{"text": "Radical Radiotherapy for Adjuvant and definitive, EBRT up to 74 Gy/37 Fractions can be given using 3DCRT or IMRT Techniques. Palliative radiotherapy is valuable to bone metastases, massive hematuria, spinal cord compression and brain "}, {"text": "metastases"}]}, {"id": "body-25119", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Hormonal Therapy", "runs": [{"text": "Hormonal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Therapy"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-25120", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Hormonal manipulation is by surgical or medical castration. It is carried out in patients with locally advanced or metastatic disease. Bilateral orchidectomy is a surgical hormonal manipulation and should not be regarded curative surgery.", "runs": [{"text": "Hormonal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "manipulation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "surgical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "castration."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "carried"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "out"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "locally"}, {"text": " "}, {"text"